MMQ tile retune for CDNA

Re-cut against upstream 030ebb558 (2026-08-10). Upstream moved the CDNA MMQ
configuration table out of mmq.cuh into its own header
(ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq-config-cdna.cuh), so the old patch no longer applied.
The stream-k change formerly shipped as patch 05 lives in the same table and is
consolidated here.

Retunes the CDNA CASE() entries from upstream's NVIDIA-derived tile choices to
shapes that suit gfx90a's 64-lane wavefronts and LDS budget.

Gate: test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT and -o MUL_MAT_ID, both fully passing
(1186/1186 and 865/865 at this base). A wrong tile config does not crash -- it
produces fluent but wrong output -- so never trust a benchmark here without the
op tests.

